<title>USA: Sumitomo's soothing words draw skepticism.</title>
<headline>Sumitomo's soothing words draw skepticism.</headline>
<byline>Huw Jones</byline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>As Sumitomo Corp's latest reassurances continued to draw scepticism among some U.S. copper brokers, it was still unclear if the scandal was now purely of historical interest or whether a market-moving legacy remained in the red metal pipeline.</p>
<p>&quot;The liquidation concerns have been alleviated and the unfolding of what exactly happened will be interesting, but more from a historical standpoint,&quot; said William O'Neill of Merrill Lynch. &quot;The impact on the market has been felt.&quot;</p>
</text>
